{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The screens that make up a scan, and how they hand over to each other."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"NewSDK"}],"title":"How a scan works","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/BaseVC","doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/ViewControllerNewCin","doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/ViewControllerNewCinVerso","doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/ViewController","doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/MainVideoViewController"],"generated":true,"anchor":"How-a-scan-works","title":"How a scan works"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/NewSDKScanner","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" creates the first screen of the flow and gives it your completion closure. Each screen passes the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure on to the next one, so it is called once, at the very end.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"New CIN"}]}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/ViewControllerNewCin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" – the front. The camera frames are analysed with ML Kit text recognition; the card fields"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are parsed from the recognised text blocks."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/ViewControllerNewCinVerso"},{"type":"text","text":" – the back. When the user confirms, the flow ends and the result is delivered."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Old CIN"}]}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/ViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" – the front. A TensorFlow Lite detector finds the six field regions on the card; each region is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cropped and read with ML Kit."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/MainVideoViewController"},{"text":" – the back. When the user confirms, the flow ends and the result is delivered.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The package also contains a selfie \/ blink screen ("},{"code":"FaceController","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/FaceDetectionView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), but the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"current flow does not present it."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All scanner screens derive from "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/BaseVC"},{"type":"text","text":", which provides the Cancel button, the scan-bar animation, the alert"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"helpers and ","type":"text"},{"code":"dismissScanFlow(animated:completion:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Dismissing the flow always closes every stacked scanner","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"screen, whichever screen the user is on."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Camera frames","type":"heading","anchor":"Camera-frames"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Frames are delivered on a background queue by "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/VideoCapture","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (or, for the old CIN front, by the camera feed manager)."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A thread-safe flag makes sure only one frame at a time is being recognised; the rest are dropped.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Time-outs","level":3,"anchor":"Time-outs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The recto screens time out after about 27 seconds (90 seconds on iPhone 6 \/ 7 class devices) and the new CIN verso","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after 27 seconds; the old CIN verso has no time-out. The new CIN front also asks the user to use an original card when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no valid card has been recognised after 7 seconds.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/newsdk\/scanflow"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/ScanFlow","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://verify2.NewSDK/documentation/NewSDK/BaseVC":{"kind":"symbol","title":"BaseVC","abstract":[{"text":"Base class of every CIN scanner screen (recto \/ verso, old and new CIN).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BaseVC"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/verify2.NewSDK\/documentation\/NewSDK\/BaseVC","url":"\/documentation\/newsdk\/basevc","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BaseVC"}]},"doc://verify2.NewSDK/documentation/NewSDK/ViewControllerNewCin":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ViewControllerNewCin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text